I know that the size makes no difference.

But I would like to ask you, whether you *know* for sure what was the 
motivation behind the original programmer's idea to make boulders sink 
at a chance of 10%.  To me, it seems very plausible that this is due to 
the idea that in reality you cannot as easily fill a large moat (or a 
deeper one for that matter, which is usually also a larger one) with 
boulders as a small one.  It is not a very realistic way to simulate 
this behaviour but a very simple one.  In any case, it has this effect - 
you will have sinking boulders more likely in big (and deep :-) ) moats 
than in small ones - on average.

Of course, as I also said, this effect could be achieved in a better 
way.  But then, the programmer may not really have thought about this at 
all...  Nevertheless, it looked like a plausible explanation to me.  If 
you happen to know that the DevTeam were not as thoughtful this time, 
that's fine with me.  If you don't know it, there is still a chance they 
were...

